/// Add memory to the system free pool
///
/// Add a new region of memory to the system free pool. The first few bytes will
/// be used to hold the MemHeader structure.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `size` - the size (in bytes) of the memory area attributes - the
///   attributes word that the memory pool will have pri - the priority for
///   this memory. CHIP memory has a pri of -10, 16 bit expansion memory
///   has a priority of 0. The higher the priority, the closer to the head
///   of the memory list it will be placed. base - the base of the new
///   memory area name - the name that will be used in the memory header,
///   or NULL if no name is to be provided. This name is not copied, so it
///   must remain valid for as long as the memory header is in the system.
///
/// See also: AllocMem, exec/memory.h
@library("exec.library")
extern pub fn AddMemList(size: u32, attributes: u32, pri: i32, base: *u8, name: *u8)
/// General purpose memory copy function
///
/// CopyMem is a general purpose, fast memory copy function. It can deal with
/// arbitrary lengths, with its pointers on arbitrary alignments.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `source` - a pointer to the source data region dest - a pointer to
///   the destination data region size - the size (in bytes) of the memory
///   area. Zero copies zero bytes
///
/// See also: CopyMemQuick
@library("exec.library")
extern pub fn CopyMem(source: *u8, dest: *u8, size: u32)
/// Optimized memory copy function
///
/// CopyMemQuick is a highly optimized memory copy function, with restrictions
/// on the size and alignment of its arguments. Both the source and destination
/// pointers must be longword aligned.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `source` - a pointer to the source data region, long aligned dest - a
///   pointer to the destination data region, long aligned size - the size
///   (in bytes) of the memory area. Zero copies zero bytes.
///
/// See also: CopyMem
@library("exec.library")
extern pub fn CopyMemQuick(source: *u8, dest: *u8, size: u32)
/// User callable simple cache clearing (V37)
///
/// Flush out the contents of any CPU instruction and data caches. If dirty data
/// cache lines are present, push them to memory first.
///
/// See also: exec/execbase.i, CacheControl, CacheClearE
@library("exec.library")
extern pub fn CacheClearU()
/// Cache clearing with extended control (V37)
///
/// Flush out the contents of the CPU instruction and/or data caches. If dirty
/// data cache lines are present, push them to memory first.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `address` - Address to start the operation. This may be rounded due
///   to hardware granularity. length - Length of area to be cleared, or
///   $FFFFFFFF to indicate all addresses should be cleared. caches - Bit
///   flags to indicate what caches to affect. The current supported flags
///   are: CACRF_ClearI ;Clear instruction cache CACRF_ClearD ;Clear data
///   cache All other bits are reserved for future definition.
///
/// See also: exec/execbase.i, CacheControl, CacheClearU
@library("exec.library")
extern pub fn CacheClearE(address: *u8, length: u32, caches: u32)
/// Instruction & data cache control
///
/// This function provides global control of any instruction or data caches that
/// may be connected to the system. All settings are global -- per task control
/// is not provided.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `cacheBits` - new values for the bits specified in cacheMask.
/// * `cacheMask` - a mask with ones for all bits to be changed.
///
/// # Returns
/// oldBits - the complete prior values for all settings.
///
/// See also: exec/execbase.i, CacheClearU, CacheClearE
@library("exec.library")
extern pub fn CacheControl(cacheBits: u32, cacheMask: u32) -> u32
